// Public entry for 'zena:wasi' — re-exports only.
//
// The guest side of the Component Model, in one library: the canonical
// ABI's string marshaling and allocator, the async-import driver that
// turns the subtask protocol into a `Future`, and the guest half of
// `stream<u8>`.
//
// Most of what is here, a Zena program never calls. The compiler
// synthesizes the wrappers that do — a lowered export's string copies,
// the entry's `finishTask`, a `stream<u8>` connected to `zena:stream`.
// The names are exported because generated code names them, and because
// infrastructure code that reaches for the component runtime directly
// has nowhere else to go.
//
// The library is all-target. The canonical ABI's marshaling is plain
// Zena, and the rest is `@external("canon", ...)` declarations, which a
// component supplies and nothing else does. Naming the module links none
// of them — reachability links one when a program calls it — so a
// wasi-family program can import this and a call it cannot honour fails
// where it is made rather than at the import.
//
// `memory.zena` sits beside these files without being re-exported: it is
// a compilation entry point the compiler builds on its own, not part of
// the library's surface.

export * from './abi.zena';
export * from './async.zena';
export * from './stream.zena';
